        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.0",
          "heading": "why_in_hospital",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.0",
            "sections.1"
          ],
          "text": "You came in with palpitations and breathlessness. The team found that your heart had gone into an irregular rhythm called atrial fibrillation (AF). Your heart was beating very fast. This had also caused some mild fluid build-up, which is a type of heart failure."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.1",
          "heading": "what_we_did",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.2",
            "sections.3"
          ],
          "text": "The team checked your pulse, blood pressure and listened to your chest. They found your heart was beating irregularly and very fast.\n\nTo slow your heart down, you were given a medicine called digoxin. Your heart rate improved. A medicine called bisoprolol was also increased.\n\nYou were also given treatment to remove the extra fluid from your body."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.2",
          "heading": "medicines",
          "source_ids": [],
          "text": "{{MEDICATIONS}}"
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.3",
          "heading": "next_steps",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.8",
            "sections.9"
          ],
          "text": "- You have a cardiology (heart specialist) follow-up appointment in 6 weeks.\n- Your GP will check your INR blood test and your digoxin level."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.4",
          "heading": "safety_net",
          "source_ids": [],
          "text": "{{SAFETY_NET}}"
        }
